# The Dockerfile only ever COPYs pom.xml, .mvn, mvnw, and src explicitly - never a blanket
# COPY . . - so nothing here can leak into the image regardless. This file exists purely to keep
# the build CONTEXT small: Render (and any Docker builder) uploads the whole context before the
# first COPY even runs, and target/ alone can be 100MB+ of stale local build output that has no
# business being sent over the network on every deploy.
target/
.idea/
*.iml
.vscode/
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
